# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the night's events
@event ev3.dusk
at: 19:08
do: set(ev3.dusk)

@event ev3.gale
at: 21:00
nar: The wind comes round the Spit and finds the town. Every loose thing in Gullet tries to leave at once.
do: set(ev3.gale)

@event ev3.vote
at: 22:30
do: set(ev3.vote_called)

@event ev3.boats_last
at: 00:00
do: set(ev3.boats_last)

@event ev3.eye
at: 00:15
camera: wide
nar: The wind stops. Not drops: stops, the way a held breath stops. The rain stops with it. Over Gullet, in a round hole in the cloud, every star there is.
do: set(ev3.eye)

@event ev3.eye_near
at: 00:17
camera: near
do: set(ev3.eye_seen)

@event ev3.eye_ends
at: 01:00
do: set(ev3.eye_ends)

@event ev3.backed
at: 01:10
nar: The wind comes back from the north-west, harder, as if it had only gone round to fetch something.
do: set(ev3.backed)

@event ev3.collier_seen
at: 03:10
do: set(ev3.collier_seen)

@event ev3.wreckers_climb
at: 03:30
do: set(ev3.wreckers_climb)

@event ev3.collier
at: 04:00
do: set(ev3.collier_turn)

@event ev3.lamps_judged
at: 04:30
when: !has(lampout.steps) & !has(lampout.porthole) & !has(lampout.gut) & !has(lampout.balance) & !has(lampout.hill) & !has(lampout.bulb) & !has(lampout.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp)
do: set(gale.lamps_held); quest(a3.lamps, kept)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- resolving the night wherever Lamb is
# (director, 2026-10-17). mole3 plays these scenes when Lamb is on the mole; these events settle
# them otherwise, and fire only when mole3 has not already set the flags.
@event ev3.wreck_mother
at: 03:55
when: !has(mole3.wreck_met) & !has(wreckers.real) & !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & (var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother)))
nar: Far out along the mole, through the rain, Mother's beam stops in the middle of a sweep, as if a hand had been put over it. It does not come back.
do: set(loss3.mother); mole3.mother = off; mole3.target = mother; quest(a3.wreckers, done)

@event ev3.wreck_steps
at: 03:55
when: !has(mole3.wreck_met) & !has(wreckers.real) & !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & !(var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother))) & var.light_steps == 1 & !has(lampout.steps)
nar: At the top of the quay steps the paraffin post goes out, not in a gust: all at once, the way a lamp goes out when somebody turns it down.
do: set(loss3.lamp); set(lampout.steps); mole3.target = lamp; quest(a3.wreckers, done)

@event ev3.wreck_balance
at: 03:55
when: !has(mole3.wreck_met) & !has(wreckers.real) & !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & !(var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother))) & var.light_balance == 1 & !has(lampout.balance) & (var.light_steps == 0 | has(lampout.steps))
nar: On the weigh-house roof the lamp on the town balance goes out all at once. A slate comes down into the street a moment later.
do: set(loss3.lamp); set(lampout.balance); mole3.target = lamp; quest(a3.wreckers, done)

@event ev3.wreck_hill
at: 03:55
when: !has(mole3.wreck_met) & !has(wreckers.real) & !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & !(var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother))) & var.light_hill == 1 & !has(lampout.hill) & (var.light_steps == 0 | has(lampout.steps)) & (var.light_balance == 0 | has(lampout.balance))
nar: Up on Chancel Hill the white lamps go out together, which they only do when somebody throws the second switch.
do: set(loss3.lamp); set(lampout.hill); mole3.target = lamp; quest(a3.wreckers, done)

@event ev3.wreck_bulb
at: 03:55
when: !has(mole3.wreck_met) & !has(wreckers.real) & !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & !(var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother))) & var.light_bulb == 1 & !has(lampout.bulb) & (var.light_steps == 0 | has(lampout.steps)) & (var.light_balance == 0 | has(lampout.balance)) & (var.light_hill == 0 | has(lampout.hill))
nar: In the gasholder frame the Old Bulb's light goes out, and the frame goes on singing in the dark.
do: set(loss3.lamp); set(lampout.bulb); mole3.target = lamp; quest(a3.wreckers, done)

@event ev3.collier_through
at: 04:05
when: !has(collier.through) & !has(collier.spit) & ((!has(loss3.mother) & (var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother)))) | (var.light_steps == 1 & !has(lampout.steps) & var.light_balance == 1 & !has(lampout.balance)) | ((has(hill3.bearing) | var.light_hill == 1) & !has(lampout.hill) & var.light_bulb == 1 & !has(lampout.bulb)) | has(oldlight.lanterns))
nar: Out at the bay's mouth the collier's lights turn, slowly, the way a large animal turns, and line up on the leading lights the town has kept. They come in through the dog-leg one after another, and the Spit is behind them.
do: set(collier.through); quest(a3.wreckers, stopped)

@event ev3.collier_spit
at: 04:05
when: !has(collier.through) & !has(collier.spit) & !((!has(loss3.mother) & (var.mole3.mother == on | (var.mole3.mother == auto & var.light_mother == 1 & !has(said.day2_mother)))) | (var.light_steps == 1 & !has(lampout.steps) & var.light_balance == 1 & !has(lampout.balance)) | ((has(hill3.bearing) | var.light_hill == 1) & !has(lampout.hill) & var.light_bulb == 1 & !has(lampout.bulb)) | has(oldlight.lanterns))
nar: Out at the bay's mouth the collier's lights come on toward the town, steering for a lamp that is not there. Then they stop moving, and lean.
do: set(collier.spit)

@event ev3.surge
at: 05:30
nar: The water is over the quay's edge and coming. Somebody is ringing the Brine's bell, the one over the bar that nobody has rung since Jory, and the whole town is going toward it.
do: set(ev3.surge)
go: brine3.surge.open

@event ev3.dawn
at: 06:20
when: !seen(dawn3.start)
go: dawn3.start
